    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that, but it feels like even when companies have the money, they spend half their time just trying to comply with a mountain of paperwork and legal hoops instead of actually building stuff. like, is there a point where the number of regulations actually starts doing more harm to the economy than the protections they're supposed to provide?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
