    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "yeah but it seems like \"safeguards\" are often just used as an excuse by big, established companies to keep newer, cheaper competitors out of the market. if the goal is actually to protect people, wouldn't it make more sense to focus on actual harm rather than creating these massive layers of oversight that just cement the status quo? it feels like the current system is basically designed to favor the giants and kill any real competition.",
